Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-16-2001||07:16 PM||||i got my battery box from the fiero store today so i decided to see where all of the spot welds are. that's when i found out that the right side of the car is rusted through where the battery box goes. after seeing the rust i decided to see where else there is rust. <P>i lifted up the carpet in the right trunk area (rear) and saw something that looks like a blower fan or something. <P>anyone know what this thing is for?<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by fiero_nightmare (edited 10-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||10-16-2001||07:19 PM||||That fan comes on( or it is supposed to) with the radiator fan. It's used to cool the coil and the alt. That's what those silver tubes are for.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||10-16-2001||07:22 PM||||The fan blows air through the "silvery" bent pipes in the engine compartment.  One pipe directs air onto the alternator, the other pipe directs air onto the ignition coil. It was a cooling effort.<P>This means you have a pre 88 V6 Fiero.  The fan turns on when the radiator fan turns on.<P>If the pipes are missing, oh well.  Som modification has been done to the car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero_nightmare||10-17-2001||08:43 AM||||thank you both for the help. i figured that is what it is but i wasn't sure and i didn't want to take anything apart to find out because i was afraid i would break something.   <P>i forgot about the tubes because i just changed engines and i had to pull the engine out the top so i took off the tubes and didn't put them back on yet.<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||7
